# Architecture Decisions — {{project_name}}

> **The project's standing decision record.** Every decision here is one another developer would
> still follow without an agent: technology choices, patterns, contract shapes, layer boundaries.
>
> This page is the CUMULATIVE surface — the reason a decision made three sessions ago is not lost.
> `context-handoff` points the next session here instead of copying decisions into a prompt,
> because this is the only place that can record that a decision was later **superseded**.
>
> **Writers:** `using-second-brain` operation 5 (DECISION CAPTURE, mid-session, asks first) and
> `finishing-a-development-branch` Step 7 item 4 (at branch close). `context-handoff` never writes
> here directly — it routes to those, so the consent gate and AD numbering stay in one place.
>
> **Decisions about how the AGENT works** (rules, skills, workflow) do NOT belong here — they go to
> `_improvement-queue/` via the `decision` signal and are reviewed with `/evolve`. The test:
> *"If a new developer joined the team without an agent, would this still apply to them?"*

